+/*
+ * FOLLOW-LIVE, the rule that replaces y2s83's freeze in MobileSlideShow once the kernel's use count is real and this texture holds it
+ * (the pool can then not hand the buffer to the next picture while the texture exists, which is all the freeze stood in for):
+ *   -1  not this rule (another process, a switch, no real use count): the y2s60..y2s83 rules decide as before;
+ *    0  keep what the texture holds: the surface's seed and probe bytes are what they were at the last conversion, OR this process's
+ *       GPU has a write of the surface in flight (committed, not completed) -- the last good conversion stays until the write's
+ *       completion moves the seed (-redwoodTouchSurface), and the next use converts the finished picture;
+ *    1  convert now: never converted, or the seed / the probe bytes moved (a decoder's write-unlock moves the seed: SweetSurface
+ *       trapUnlock without kIOSurfaceLockReadOnly; this process's GPU writes move it at completion: compute (y2s60) and, y2s91,
+ *       render passes into a YCbCr plane).
+ * No timing rule (no "young" 3 s, no "finished" luma row, no 3 s give-up).
+ */
+- (int)redwoodTGLiveDecision
+{
+	struct rw_ycbcr_planes pl;
+
